#
# Without this file the build context is the whole repository — every
# node_modules, the git history, and `data/`, which is the user's
# (docs/design/workplan/19-p6a-alpha-1.md §0.6). Three of the entries below are
# not about size.

# The user's data. It is canonical, it is theirs, and it must never be baked
# into an image (docs/design/03-data-model.md §5).
data/
config.json
captures/
logs/
.env
.env.local

# Build output. The image builds its own; a stale local `dist` reaching the
# context would be silently preferred over the one this build made.
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/dist-types/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
coverage/
.vite/
.vitest/

# **The identity, specifically.** `readBuildInfo` reads
# `packages/server/build-info.json`, and the image writes its own from the
# commit it was told. A developer's local one arriving in the context would
# claim the image is a build it is not — which is the one lie this whole phase
# exists to prevent (§1.5).
packages/server/build-info.json

# Not source, and not needed to build.
.git/
.github/
.claude/
docs/
deploy/
*.md
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
